# HAL's brain settings. Copy this file to brain/.env (which git ignores) and edit it there.
# `tools/brain.sh pair` creates brain/.env by itself if you haven't.

# The key shared with HAL Zero. Leave it out: `tools/brain.sh pair` makes one and puts it here.
# Without a key the brain only answers requests from this computer.
# HAL_BRAIN_KEY=

HAL_BRAIN_PORT=9100

# Which model writes the HALs' lines. ollama runs on this computer: nothing leaves the house.
HAL_BRAIN_PROVIDER=ollama
HAL_BRAIN_MODEL=qwen3.6:35b-a3b

# --- Optional: Claude or ChatGPT instead (docs/SETUP.md, step 9) -------------------------
# With one of these, every line sends that company the HAL's instructions, the facts he knows,
# the last few lines of the chat and your question. Recordings never leave this computer.
# To use one, remove the two lines above and take the '#' off its three lines below.
#
# Claude (a model of the 5 series). First: tools/.venv/bin/pip install anthropic
# HAL_BRAIN_PROVIDER=claude
# HAL_BRAIN_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#
# ChatGPT. Name one of OpenAI's models: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models
# HAL_BRAIN_PROVIDER=openai
# HAL_BRAIN_MODEL=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
